<title>GERMANY: Smaller firms deserve access to ECB loans - Zeitler.</title>
<headline>Smaller firms deserve access to ECB loans - Zeitler.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler on Tuesday said smaller- and medium-sized firms ought to have access to credit facilities from the future European Central Bank (ECB).</p>
<p>In the text of a speech to be delivered at a conference in Italy, Zeitler said smaller firms not active on money markets should be able to access ECB credits &quot;to avoid making them dependent on large commercial banks.&quot;</p>
<p>The ECB should thus offer a longer-term basis refinancing instrument as well as short-term instruments, Zeitler said.</p>
<p>A summary of his speech was made available in Frankfurt in advance.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
